                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "This game is kind of the definition of a mixed bag, It has quite a few good things or cool ideas but it also has a lot of failures or overall just negative things about it.\nAs a Berserk fan I am biased towards this game, especially due to it being one of the only official Berserk games out there.\n\nPros:\n\nThe combat is fun and feels really nice: Fighting big crowds of enemies and hearing the sounds as you just cut them to shreds is really fun and cool to do.\n\nThe animated segments are a fun thing for the game, even thought they weren't MADE for the game, it is still a good thing.\n\nThe graphics are perfect for a Berserk game in my opinion.\nThe different selection of characters makes for a pretty fun time going through previous missions with the new unlocks.\n\nCons:\nThe combat gets repetitive quite damn fast. After the Zodd boss fight, there's basically never really anything new added to the combat at all, even new moves you unlock with levels feel worthless due to the way they work. Will go more into details on the moves later.\n\nThe animated segments stop half way through the game. After a bit of the story there's no longer any 2d animated segments and it just goes to basic cutscenes, which are nice but it just feels so weird switching between them randomly.\nNot having Skull Knight as a playable character but having a moveset for his NPC is just kind of dumb.\n\nMaps are reused quite a few times. Throughout the game you will notice that you've already been on that map before. It just feels really cheap that quite a few maps are completely re used with 0 differences, most of the time the only  difference being certain parts of the map are blocked off\n\nThe new moves you unlock feel completely worthless. You gain levels while playing through the game, those levels giving new moves for the character. Only issue is those moves are useless. Like, there's no point in using a move that uses more inputs when moves you get after a few levels of the game are still really good late game, especially with the extra weapons you can bring using the variety of moves just doesn't feel needed and never really is.\n\nThe controls/inputs are terrible. Every review basically says this, the controls for the game on PC are bad. To go over the PC controls quickly, you have to move the camera around with keys, you can't use the mouse to move the camera at all, which makes it feel really tedious, especially with how SLOW the camera moves anyway. Not only that, but the entire game still shows the inputs as a controller, so you have to go search through the settings just to learn how to do it on PC. Using a controller is basically the only way to enjoy the gameplay a bit.\n\nThe inputs to use moves is just boring and extremely repetitive. To start with you have 2 types of moves you can do, a normal attack and a heavy attack that you can charge up, that's 2 buttons, you might think that as you unlock more moves you use more buttons to use better moves in like sequences, but nope. Every move you unlock just requires an extra input of one of the 2 buttons. If you want to do the 2nd normal attack, just press normal attack twice. If you wanna do a special heavy attack you have to do normal attack then 2 heavy attacks. And that's what EVERY MOVE you get is, with every one of the moves requiring one more input, so to use the last attacks you have to press light attack like 7 times and heavy attack twice. It just feels really bad just pressing the same 2 buttons to attack the entire time. The items could've been a way to help this but the items have extremely long cds or are just boring attacks like a simple knife throw.\n\nHorse combat is horrible. A lot of missions want you to attack while riding a horse, but the horse mechanics are so damn clunky, you can only do a basic attack on a horse, the horse has it's special heavy attack which has it's own problems. But the basic attacks will only hit one side of the horse, so you have to basically run around in circles continuously attacking just hoping you kill the enemies, which sometimes just wont happen since the hitboxes are bad. The horses heavy attack is a charge, where the horse runs at a high speed and crashes through enemies. Issue is, it only works if there's no enemies around you, otherwise the horse just stands there and slams down which gets you hit. Even just the movement on the horse feels really clunky because you're expected to do sharp corners but with how slow the camera is, it's nearly impossible without having to slow down to a snail pace.\n\nThe boss fights just feel so soulless. At most a boss will have like 5 attacks that they'll throw at you in a really easy to see pattern, to the point they're not really a danger or even fun to fight against. The only bosses that are KIND OF fun to fight are the giant bosses, even still they have the issue of being able to bypass literally anything you throw at them meaning you kind of just have to tank all their hits as you fight. \n\nOverall: I cannot recommend this game to anyone, even to die hard Berserk fans I just can't, especially for the absurd price of the game. I got it on sale for nearly half price and I still feel like that was too much money for what this is, it has some good things about it but the main issues lie within the foundation of the game itself, stuff that can't be overlooked but are instead right in front of your eyes the entire time, the game is such a good concept just it has too many issues for me to be able to tell anyone to buy it. Wish it was good but it just isn't.",
